    "C06","C13","C14",
    "C07","C03",
    "C102","C90","C79","C54","C101","C100","C91","C57"
  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Pethidine, which shares the query's 4-phenylpiperidine core, had systemic availability 0.80 ± 0.15 in cirrhosis and about 0.48 in normal subjects; L2 records confirm 0.80–0.87 in cirrhosis, all well above 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C05","C19","C23","C47","C52"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Setipiprant, a carboxylic acid-containing drug, had human F of at least 50%; L2 rat/dog F values of 44% and 55% support that the acid group does not preclude F ≥ 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C11","C27","C34","C36","C37"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Odanacatib, containing nitrile and fluorophenyl motifs, had absolute F of 70% at 10 mg and 30% at 50 mg; L2 relative F estimates at 10–50 mg were 40–82%, all above 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C02","C09","C25","C26","C28"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Maraviroc fasted F was 24% at 100 mg and 33% at 600 mg, above threshold; dose dependence does not create affirmative low evidence.",
      "card_ids": ["C12","C22","C44","C50"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records for structurally related acids/zwitterions show measurable oral Cmax/AUC: cilomilast (same nitrile-cyclohexane-carboxylic acid motif) reached Cmax 1.70–3.05 µg/mL and AUC0-12 6.5–21.5 µg·h/mL across 7–30 mg BID; sparfloxacin AUC was 35 µg·h/mL; temafloxacin Cmax was 4.07 mg/L after 600 mg; ketorolac Cmax was 1.14 µg/mL after 10 mg and AUC 12.5 µg/mL·h after 30 mg; flumequine Cmax was 8 µg/mL after 400 mg in humans.",
      "card_ids": ["C102","C90","C79","C54","C101","C100","C91","C57"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The only sub-20% F record, ampicillin in veal calves (12%), is species-specific and not transferable to the human/query prediction.",
      "card_ids": ["C31"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "oral_auc_cmax_exposure",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C102","C90","C79","C54","C101","C100","C91","C57"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule; prediction remains transfer-based.",
    "L3 exposure records lack IV comparators, so they show oral absorption/exposure but do not quantify F directly.",
    "Query condition is unspecified; many high-F contexts are fasted or cirrhosis, and pethidine normal F (~0.48) is above threshold but not an exact condition match.",
    "The query is a zwitterion with logD -0.74 and neutral fraction 0 at pH 7.4; passive permeability may be limited, and no experimental permeability or transporter data are available.",
    "Odanacatib L2 F1 values are relative, not absolute, and dose-dependent; maraviroc F is also dose-dependent, so quantitative transfer is uncertain.",
    "Animal L2 data (setipiprant, ampicillin calves) may not translate quantitatively to humans."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L3 oral exposure records for structurally related acids/zwitterions (cilomilast, sparfloxacin, temafloxacin, ketorolac, flumequine) show measurable oral Cmax/AUC, supporting absorption of the query's acid/zwitterion and nitrile-cyclohexane motifs. They do not provide direct F values, but they reinforce the L1/L2 transferable F evidence (pethidine, setipiprant, odanacatib, maraviroc, meptazinol, haloperidol, ketanserin, glasdegib), all above 20%. The only sub-20% record is species-specific calf ampicillin and is not transferable. Prediction remains high with moderate confidence."
}

